{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790450529,"nonce":"ZuDzesW/qSiCjP5dOA+8zJhliVY=","title":"wasm AOT: hatch plugins as finished modules the harness links at load","message":"A wasm AOT build refuses foreign classes and bundled native libraries.\nHatch's wasm plugins (hatch-window, hatch-gpu, hatch-hello) ship as\nfinished cdylib modules with their own memory, which the browser harness\n(wasm/web/wlift.js) instantiates beside the runtime: their env imports\nare the runtime's exports plus the wlift_get_slot_str/wlift_set_slot_str\nbridges that copy strings between the two memories, and calls reach them\nthrough the dynamic dispatch import. An AOT program takes the runtime's\nplace in that scheme; plugins keep their format.\n\nBuild (wlift --aot --aot-target wasm32-*):\n- Foreign classes bind through wlift_aot_bind_foreign_class as on\n  native, resolving each #!symbol to a dynamic plugin index.\n- The program's plugin modules (the wasm variant of each NativeLib) ride\n  in the output as custom sections, one per library, so the program stays\n  one file.\n- The linker exports what the harness and plugins need: memory, the\n  wren* functions each plugin imports (read from its import section),\n  wlift_host_alloc/free and wlift_register_plugin_dynamic_export.\n\nRuntime (aot_runtime on wasi): dispatch_dynamic calls a plain import,\nwlift.plugin_dispatch(idx, vm), in place of the wasm-bindgen one.\n\nHarness: instantiate the program without starting it, instantiate each\nplugin against the program's exports plus the two string bridges,\nregister each wlift_* export, then call _start.\n- tests/wasm_aot.rs does this under embedded wasmtime.\n- wlift.js loads an AOT program in place of the runtime module.\n- A WASI host for the command line (plain wasmtime cannot link two\n  modules).\n\nPlugins keep building as they do; nothing changes for plugin authors.","files":null}]}